 "lemmaTab": "⊆",
 "introduction":
 "How do you prove that one set is a subset of another?  To prove that `A ⊆ B`,\nyou have to show that if some object `x` is an element of `A`, then it is also\nan element of `B`.  To do that, you'll have to introduce an object called `x` into\nthe proof.  The object denoted by `x` could be anything, so we say that it\nis *arbitrary*.\n\nIn this level, we start with a simple example of this kind of proof.  We're going\nto show that if `A` is a set, then `A ⊆ A`.",
 "index": 5,
 "image": "",
 "displayName": "Subset.refl",
 "descrText": "Let $A$ be any set.  Then $A \\subseteq A$.",
 "descrFormat": "theorem Subset.refl (A : Set U) : A ⊆ A  := by",
